# Supabase Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your Supabase credentials
# 
# To get your Supabase credentials:
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com and create a project (or use an existing one)
# 2. Go to Project Settings > API
# 3. Copy the "Project URL" and "anon public" key

NUXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NUXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Note: The app can work without Supabase for local-only development
# (uses IndexedDB/localStorage for data persistence)

# FC View Logbook API (server-only; set after receiving access from FC View portal)
#
# Required for /api/fcv/auth (otherwise returns 503 “not configured”):
#   FCV_CLIENT_ID, FCV_CLIENT_SECRET, FCV_REDIRECT_URI, FCV_AUTHORIZE_URL, FCV_TOKEN_URL
# Also required for FC View API calls after connect:
#   FCV_API_BASE_URL
# Callback stores tokens in Supabase — set:
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
# On Vercel: Project → Settings → Environment Variables → add all of the above → redeploy.
# Enable each variable for Preview (branch deployments) if you test on *.vercel.app URLs — not Production-only.
# The API resolves FCV_* from the live environment at request time (and accepts NUXT_FCV_* aliases).
#
# FCV_CLIENT_ID=
# FCV_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Redirect URI must match EXACTLY what is registered in the FC View OAuth client (scheme, host, port, path).
# FC View requires redirect URIs to start with https:// (http://localhost is rejected in their UI).
# For local dev, serve Nuxt over HTTPS with mkcert, then register and use:
#   FCV_REDIRECT_URI=https://localhost:3000/api/fcv/callback
# Steps:
#   1. Install mkcert, then trust its CA: `mkcert -install`
#      - With Homebrew: `brew install mkcert` (install Homebrew from https://brew.sh if needed).
#        After a fresh Homebrew install, `brew` is not on PATH until you run the “Next steps” it prints,
#        e.g. `eval "$(/opt/homebrew/bin/brew shellenv zsh)"` (Apple Silicon; Intel Mac often `/usr/local/bin/brew`),
#        or run once: `/opt/homebrew/bin/brew install mkcert`
#      - Without Homebrew (macOS): in Terminal run `uname -m` — arm64 = Apple Silicon, x86_64 = Intel.
#        Apple Silicon:
#          mkdir -p ~/bin && curl -sL -o ~/bin/mkcert https://github.com/FiloSottile/mkcert/releases/download/v1.4.4/mkcert-v1.4.4-darwin-arm64 && chmod +x ~/bin/mkcert
#        Intel Mac:
#          mkdir -p ~/bin && curl -sL -o ~/bin/mkcert https://github.com/FiloSottile/mkcert/releases/download/v1.4.4/mkcert-v1.4.4-darwin-amd64 && chmod +x ~/bin/mkcert
#        Add to ~/.zshrc:  export PATH="$HOME/bin:$PATH"
#        Then:  source ~/.zshrc  and  mkcert -install
#      More options: https://github.com/FiloSottile/mkcert#installation
#   2. mkdir -p logifi.web/certs && cd logifi.web/certs
#   3. Generate certs (entire line — do not run `mkcert -key-file` alone):
#        mkcert -key-file localhost-key.pem -cert-file localhost.pem localhost 127.0.0.1
#      Or: `mkcert localhost 127.0.0.1` then use the printed *.pem names in NUXT_DEV_HTTPS_* below.
#   4. In .env:
# NUXT_DEV_HTTPS_KEY=certs/localhost-key.pem
# NUXT_DEV_HTTPS_CERT=certs/localhost.pem
#   5. Open https://localhost:3000 (not http) and run `npm run dev`
# Production:
# FCV_REDIRECT_URI=https://your-app.com/api/fcv/callback
# FCV_TOKEN_URL=
# FCV_AUTHORIZE_URL=
# FCV_API_BASE_URL=

# Optional: Supabase service role key (required for FC View OAuth callback to store tokens server-side)
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
